-- Per-session rows for ANONYMOUS players in the operator view.
--
-- This replaces counts-only reporting (0021), at the operator's explicit request:
-- seeing that "3 guests are connected" does not answer the question actually being
-- asked during an incident, which is whether a given session is idle, sitting in a
-- lobby, or in a match.
--
-- WHAT THE IDENTIFIER IS, because it is the whole privacy question here: the
-- server's own per-socket connection id. It is generated by this process to route
-- messages, is not derived from anything about the person (no IP, no fingerprint),
-- is written nowhere else, and dies with the socket — a reconnect produces an
-- unrelated id. It distinguishes one live session from another RIGHT NOW without
-- being able to follow anyone between sessions.
--
-- Still a snapshot: overwritten by the next beat, gone when the machine goes quiet.
-- The privacy policy states all of this; if this column's contents ever widen,
-- that text has to move with it.
alter table presence add column if not exists guests jsonb not null default '[]'::jsonb;
